SRC_001's mechanism is impossible under the stated dynamics. When a vertex flips, the number of crossing edges incident to it changes by 3 - 2k, where k is the number of neighbors of the opposite color. A flip occurs only when k >= 2, so the change is -1 (k=2) or -3 (k=3). Thus the cut size is a strictly decreasing Lyapunov function until no vertex has k >= 2. There is no unbiased or mean-reverting walk in cut density, no positive fixed point rho* ~ 0.08, and no Ornstein-Uhlenbeck fluctuations around it. The claimed exp(-Theta(sqrt(n))) absorption from an OU process is not the dynamics of this model.

